                <pb facs="0413" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 895.52/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your January 23. In an interview I had with him to-day the minister for foreign
                    affairs declared that land titles of foreigners will be carefully respected and
                    that consular registrations will be treated as prima facie valid. He will make
                    formal replies without delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
